:answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310418} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c2cd7e-7dc6-594e-b28b-77490d3513fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "312bf705-0322-512f-9e06-34cf1b93dcf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309119} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4c45c37-a023-53c3-ac8e-d4201d7ee14f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1b58dd-d9eb-5759-b200-6a40e1aaa8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309095} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8f3b34-13ee-52fb-a1af-ec369edc2187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309467} {:answer/id #uuid "9683dd3c-7513-5249-90cd-03ae51c967d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309953} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a58b64-5aee-5dcd-91f8-3e6c8600c520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310201} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3fb1f9-5e91-5a7a-bc06-3c46d8a954ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e1b58dd-d9eb-5759-b200-6a40e1aaa8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309095} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4e56fcc-74b8-5f27-abf5-5b0786ac27bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1779cd6b-e209-53e3-8f4f-5bba29090ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308933} {:answer/id #uuid "33987127-5ef9-5c93-a731-5e687b762115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309141} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea2c75b-5361-5842-9114-04ecca88c736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309603} {:answer/id #uuid "a3ee95c9-1cd6-5871-bb8e-20252dbb75a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33987127-5ef9-5c93-a731-5e687b762115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309141} :answer-field/id #uuid "f65f0ce5-d1f3-5655-a171-39abea665684" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9a8802d-3d4d-5564-8390-a80c9704bb8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-337133" :question/problem "Consider the following inexact differential equation.\n\n$$\nx\\,\\text{d}y-y\\,\\text{d}x=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below about whether $I(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{3}}$ is an integrating factor of this equation.\n\nTo show that $I(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{3}}$ is an integrating factor for the given differential equation, we need to check if the following equation is exact:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=0\n$$\n\nFor this equation, let's denote\n\n$$\nP=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}},\\,Q=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-2}},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{{field-4}},\n$$\n\nthe transformed equation {{field-5}} exact.\n\nTherefore, $I(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{3}}$ {{field-6}} an integrating factor for the initial differential equation." :question/worked-solution "A function $I(x,y)$ is an integrating factor for the differential equation\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nif the following equation is exact:\n\n$$\nI(x,y)[P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y]=0\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to check if the following equation is exact:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{3}}(x\\,\\text{d}y-y\\,\\text{d}x) & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our transformed equation, we have  \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\right)=-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\right)=-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x},\n$$\n\nthe transformed equation $\\text{is}$ exact.\n\nTherefore, $I(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{3}}$ $\\text{is}$ an integrating factor for the initial differential equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217795 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "914ca4b0-99e1-5daa-b903-a2962ae29190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(xe^{y})dx + ((y + x)e^{y})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216623} {:answer/id #uuid "a414c210-0e44-5a7e-ac93-373fc8dce431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{y}dx + (\\frac{y}{e^{y}} + e^{y})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216624} {:answer/id #uuid "12fb0738-a05b-58dd-b651-f30e143a29be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((y + x)e^{y})dx + (xe^{y})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216625} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffbf1a1-5698-5917-8f9f-3377137241fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{y}{e^{y}} + e^{y})dx + e^{y}dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216626}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f295554a-7737-5d80-a713-a287a322a8bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216622}] :question/id #uuid "12ada104-bb4c-5d87-b191-73ff3d715709" :question/math-academy-id "q-337143" :question/problem "Consider the following inexact differential equation.\n\n$(y + x)dx + xdy = 0$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below about whether $I(y) = e^{y}$ is an integrating factor of this equation.\n\nTo show that the function $I(y) = e^{y}$ is an integrating factor for the given differential equation, we need to check if the following equation is exact:\n\n$(xe^{y})dx + ((y + x)e^{y})dy$ {{field-1}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95464093-5756-5884-9558-6338e21ec323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216628} {:answer/id #uuid "3568c03e-dc4f-5c87-a558-6c512e93eea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216629} {:answer/