ield-1}} where $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, then an integrating factor for the equation is\n$\\exp (-\\intg(x)dx)$ {{field-2}}\nwhere $\\exp (x)$ denotes the exponential function $e^{x}$.Let's denote\n$P(x, y) = - (4xy - 7x), Q(x, y) = 1$.Now, we compute the partial derivatives:$-4x$ {{field-3}} $1$ {{field-4}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe79229-b897-5734-b91a-f3c63ec417ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} + \\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216647} {:answer/id #uuid "00fb048b-5746-500b-b37c-5cb3f2e852f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} - \\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216648} {:answer/id #uuid "0267deed-88e3-53e2-93ba-7ccb0c5e9af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} + \\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216649} {:answer/id #uuid "285737c8-90ce-5eba-abbe-79e4db6fbe3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} - \\frac{∂Q}{∂x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216650}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0476d3-1816-5b7f-b74e-4fc918148e2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a6e2481-3c82-55b7-8499-3e02e4b84773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\"\\exp (h(y))\", \"\\exp (-h(y))\"" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216652} {:answer/id #uuid "3a997d43-0d80-5700-a892-a02cd4718372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\exp (-\\inth(y)dy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216653} {:answer/id #uuid "48b93503-a13c-5228-ae15-fd7e862e