r/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309841} {:answer/id #uuid "8d77dbc5-3e18-5e63-a111-a5e57377ccde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309866} {:answer/id #uuid "c54e10be-0055-52c4-b00e-9e4ecedb0ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d77dbc5-3e18-5e63-a111-a5e57377ccde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309866} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd3b410-36ae-578b-9aac-506893c5792e" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b8d74e8-a54f-5be1-a6d2-2f5ebd3fa9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309584} {:answer/id #uuid "a656822c-a72c-5ba1-b043-5195f3e770d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310089} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a53739-d967-59dd-adb3-336c37c133a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310256} {:answer/id #uuid "cffa6d5c-957f-503d-af49-127a1f9a50c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b8d74e8-a54f-5be1-a6d2-2f5ebd3fa9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309584} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3de92ac-9f60-55ca-a554-a263ddd62fcd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "42e6c1cc-5e39-58f3-8e83-e08cd740c8f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-337476" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3y-2\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2-3y,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $x$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\n(2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2-3y,\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2-3y)=-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{1}(-3-0) \\\\  & =-3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-3x) \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(x)\\cdot ((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=I(x)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{e}^{-3x}\\cdot ((2-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97389f4c-07a5-5c39-bdf0-5d7571e2acde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-g(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309960} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b2908a-570b-5ecd-909a-c1c5dc7c6052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310069} {:answer/id #uuid "b58f92b4-92a6-5607-ae96-cb9a781cef55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310215} {:answer/id #uuid "e99371e3-5711-5e17-a7c0-c6664c29208a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(g(x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b58f92b4-92a6-5607-ae96-cb9a781cef55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310215} :answer-field/id #uuid "110db125-bc83-561d-b67d-3eb3f31bfb0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759