:answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-({y}^{3}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310640} {:answer/id #uuid "f5501100-5f69-5621-bccf-877b8a6db1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5501100-5f69-5621-bccf-877b8a6db1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310699} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc26f1a9-2294-5423-a66b-889e19f78e81" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45f662e8-542b-5be9-816b-1defdf22619f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309284} {:answer/id #uuid "64ad37e6-739d-5ef7-96c6-1a6c1d98b828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309523} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6aa404-eaf3-550e-93a2-45e9996142df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310274} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8908fc-0913-50d5-9ce4-15acfd6cdd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45f662e8-542b-5be9-816b-1defdf22619f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f10a106b-ae20-5011-a556-104dc38d854a" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e724372-1748-58b7-9601-c50906401bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({y}^{3}+1)(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308978} {:answer/id #uuid "86003a6c-5193-5af9-9edc-5d9430b865b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309794} {:answer/id #uuid "98af1f00-b7e2-5276-97e7-b34eb2cd80fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3y}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309978} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f51c5f-4184-57b1-a82a-cd4444a19cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-({y}^{3}+1)}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86003a6c-5193-5af9-9edc-5d9430b865b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309794} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41b1634-09e9-5ef2-884f-41911521ab81" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dbfd1646-4161-5287-89b4-1be0e0c83510" :question/math-academy-id "q-337707" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}{y}^{′}=-x{y}^{3}-x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\nx({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x({y}^{3}+1))=3x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{x({y}^{3}+1)}(3x{y}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{3}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(y)\\cdot (x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=I(y)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6646f4ad-3070-5d5e-a73e-a8c9aa4bf957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309535} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba2a543-9f5b-5df6-9537-ee8be82e0bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309851} {:answer/id #uuid "c2aea39e-077a-58bd-94f8-dcd87e82da37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310310} {:answer/id #uuid "f7abe7b7-5969-551b-a9f2-5bf72b123aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7abe7b7-5969-551b-a9f2-5bf72b123aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310718} :answer-field/id #uuid "40e4286d-736e-5a47-98a2-d5df445a7847" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9849d753-4231-5961-a0a9-0b8eebe191ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}-5y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309974} {:answer/id #uuid "9a74e47f-d900-5fd7-949b-844833fa12f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}-5{y}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309998} {:answer/id #uuid "d1848d46-5e76-5a3a-9842-b825578153fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-5y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310432} {:answer/id #uuid "f2af46e2-c00d-5e52-8c4e-3e6522464657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{3}}-5y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1848d46-5e76-5a3a-9842-b825578153fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-5y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310432} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac807c8-917b-5f37-9a1e-f53b5aaaf652" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2024595f-0932-52b3-a267-c0301403f4b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-338070" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\nxy\\,\\text{d}x-({x}^{2}+5{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{3}{y}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=xy,\\,Q(x,y)=-{x}^{2}-5{y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(y)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{3}{y}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{3}{y}$ is a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that the integrating factor for the equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x,y) & ={e}^{-\\int 3/y\\text{ }\\text{d}y} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our equation by the integrating factor, we arrive at the following exact differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(yx\\,\\text{d}x-({x}^{2}+5{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y) & =0 \\\\ \\underbrace{\\left(\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\right)}_{\\overset{~}{P}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\underbrace{(-1)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}+5)}_{\\overset{~}{Q}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor this exact equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}},\\,\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}-5.\n$$\n\nTo solve the equation, let's first integrate $\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $y,$ which we'll call $F(y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{P}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}+F(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's integrate $\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $x,$ which we'll call $G(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}-5)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-5y+G(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\nF(y)=-5y,\\,G(x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-5y=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314742 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aedd9bd-ed1a-5e77-b2f7-f30da0a5f713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312306} {:answer/id #uuid "57ccbd57-fa23-559b-98b8-b5e841180c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312681} {:answer/id #uuid "cdef54e5-6300-5adf-8b67-f67f3d6adf19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313582} {:answer/id #uuid "e84e2fcb-966f-50fe-933a-7d7bca5b43cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e84e2fcb-966f-50fe-933a-7d7bca5b43cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313823} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c06983b-ddc0-5fb8-876c-9a1b2e5a5d20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e2552c-69a6-579e-bbf1-16c8783aa693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312231} {:answer/id #uuid "570993af-0477-5d4a-a51a-93ab09600014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312675} {:answer/id #uuid "8abc34ec-135c-55d0-9650-b60ad2fb71aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313078} {:answer/id #uuid "fbced680-9552-56f6-9aa0-2c4c50f109b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}-y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8abc34ec-135c-55d0-9650-b60ad2fb71aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313078} :answer-field/id #uuid "53b72e68-7474-5f06-9316-c9731a3be22e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3e13738f-f5b5-5418-9627-22b39e555f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-338870" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{2}{y}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}y,\\,Q(x,y)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-{y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(y)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{2}{y}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{2}{y}$ is a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that the integrating factor for the equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x,y) & ={e}^{-\\int 2/y\\text{ }\\text{d}y} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our equation by the integrating factor, we arrive at the following exact differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}({x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y) & =0 \\\\ \\underbrace{\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\right)}_{\\overset{~}{P}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\underbrace{(-1)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3{y}^{2}}+y)}_{\\overset{~}{Q}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor this exact equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y},\\,\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3{y}^{2}}-y.\n$$\n\nTo solve the equation, let's first integrate $\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $y,$ which we'll call $F(y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{P}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3y}+F(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's integrate $\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $x,$ which we'll call $G(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3{y}^{2}}-y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+G(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\nF(y)=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2},\\,G(x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abf24ac1-14c8-59af-bdf5-a848b7e16312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}-3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385232} {:answer/id #uuid "1d526967-d79e-5a3d-a372-309ae75e7306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385233} {:answer/id #uuid "84ac26a9-6b6f-5210-ae4f-b9cd70408dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}}-3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385234} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3e35e6-8dae-5b98-b18c-d7ff314d7f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3{y}^{3}}-3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d526967-d79e-5a3d-a372-309ae75e7306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385233} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fda5882-9553-56c8-a52d-488fa92cd5c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09177831-814c-5971-b624-41414e9b0472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385237} {:answer/id #uuid "aed9c0ec-7ee9-50a7-a3ef-396019c0e024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385238} {:answer/id #uuid "2103b7a3-69ca-5342-be52-1d522811c14b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385239} {:answer/id #uuid "070815bd-b211-5b44-87d7-3fd76aa66a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09177831-814c-5971-b624-41414e9b0472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385237} :answer-field/id #uuid "4161da91-eb9d-5d74-bfe6-181d817d6163" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "91806f1a-e750-5e85-a659-666c818f545f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337679" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\nxy\\,\\text{d}x-({x}^{2}+3{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{3}{y}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=xy,\\,Q(x,y)=-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(y)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{3}{y}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{3}{y}$ is a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that the integrating factor for the equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x,y) & ={e}^{-\\int 3/y\\text{ }\\text{d}y} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our equation by the integrating factor, we arrive at the following exact differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(xy\\,\\text{d}x-({x}^{2}+3{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y) & =0 \\\\ \\underbrace{\\left(\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\right)}_{\\overset{~}{P}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\underbrace{(-1)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}+3)}_{\\overset{~}{Q}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor this exact equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}},\\,\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}-3.\n$$\n\nTo solve the equation, let's first integrate $\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $y,$ which we'll call $F(y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{P}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}+F(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's integrate $\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $x,$ which we'll call $G(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}-3)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-3y+G(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\nF(y)=-3y,\\,G(x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}}-3y=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "405a5785-5b34-57dd-8ee6-7cf3c14c3b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391656} {:answer/id #uuid "02c9e893-9d91-5235-b549-382b71a5543f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391657} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc97e04-8bc1-5d35-bd81-38e3fca740d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391658} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9976bc-fa6f-5d35-a147-d160f45c0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc97e04-8bc1-5d35-bd81-38e3fca740d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391658} :answer-field/id #uuid "20192922-8171-54fa-90a2-ddc855fb0da5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7efa86-b472-5ed5-b224-1426be141770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391661} {:answer/id #uuid "28cb4cfd-dc4e-58e9-9682-e66719264ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391662} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2aa6bc-5f1f-5b98-a317-03dc20826446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391663} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcc8170-82d1-59e4-8e50-50028abda132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdcc8170-82d1-59e4-8e50-50028abda132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391664} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb50e09f-3243-5b20-805e-de37af2e1718" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5b12f52-bca9-597a-88b5-c5036d3e9da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-338027" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3x+{y}^{2},\\,Q(x,y)=xy+\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\,$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{1}{x}$ is a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that the integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int {x}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our equation by the integrating factor, we arrive at the following exact differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x[(3x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}y] & =0 \\\\ \\underbrace{(3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})}_{\\overset{~}{P}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\underbrace{({x}^{2}y+3)}_{\\overset{~}{Q}}\\,\\text{d}y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor this exact equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2},\\,\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)={x}^{2}y+3.\n$$\n\nTo solve the equation, let's first integrate $\\overset{~}{P}(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $y,$ which we'll call $F(y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{P}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+F(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+F(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's integrate $\\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$\nThe result should include an arbitrary function of $x,$ which we'll call $G(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int \\overset{~}{Q}(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{2}y+3)\\,\\text{d}y+G(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y+G(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we must have\n\n$$\nF(y)=3y,\\,G(x)={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+3y=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186680845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e8e68c-6209-5796-ae68-32adf801f1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680832} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8b78e5-89d7-5e95-9336-8058b91dd444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680853} {:answer/id #uuid "b670a4c1-2470-56bf-97eb-b2e6610406cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680867} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d59982-2607-5c92-b82d-cbccd6d0ac27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8b78e5-89d7-5e95-9336-8058b91dd444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680853} :answer-field/id #uuid "6906391b-2b35-570d-a938-75f0ce390d76" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ff694d-40a0-5c3b-8e76-764dd154f27c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^2\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2x\\,\\mathrm{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186680835} {:answer/id #uuid "1d9423b6-8801-539e-99b1-a1eae9d92501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^2\\,\\mathr