 "2y(y^2+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681042} {:answer/id #uuid "9661957a-a34b-5475-b8eb-81aa29e3f5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{y^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681063} {:answer/id #uuid "dbbc6021-f329-5510-8ffc-9d168adce4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{y^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbbc6021-f329-5510-8ffc-9d168adce4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{y^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681086} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc1c5ac-7455-586c-bdd4-d850fb7ac729" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d29a6ab-40a7-524f-a945-47f820140c7a" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor depending only on $y$ for\n\n$$\ny\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-x(y^2+1),\\qquad x>0,\\ y>0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options to complete the reasoning.\n\nFor an equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\ndepends only on $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nHere $\\exp(u)=e^u$.\n\nFirst rewrite the given equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet $P$ be the coefficient of $\\mathrm{d}x$ and $Q$ the coefficient of $\\mathrm{d}y$ in that form. Compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nThe ratio is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nwhich depends only on $y$. Therefore\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplying the differential equation by this factor gives\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Move the right side to the left and multiply by $\\mathrm{d}x$:\n\n$$\nx(y^2+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+y\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nThus $P=x(y^2+1)$ and $Q=y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=2xy,\\qquad Q_x=0 \\\\ h(y)&=\\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}=\\frac{2xy}{x(y^2+1)}=\\frac{2y}{y^2+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $x>0$ permits cancellation of $x$, and the ratio depends only on $y$. Use the negative integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\frac{2y}{y^2+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\ln(y^2+1)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{y^2+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the integral, use $u=y^2+1$ and $\\mathrm{d}u=2y\\,\\mathrm{d}y$; also $y^2+1>0$. We choose the constant multiplier to be $1$. The exact equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{1}{y^2+1}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad x(y^2+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+y\\,\\mathrm{d}y] =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\nx\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\frac{y}{y^2+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nBoth cross-partials are $0$, verifying exactness."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39fe65bd-2587-5dfc-b399-2351da185ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^y}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681034} {:answer/id #uuid "8e65e417-8eb5-5e3d-b8b4-61fccdf2de6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681061} {:answer/id #uuid "b9328f7c-d50e-50b0-ab1d-da1fb71fe083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ye^{-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681071} {:answer/id #uuid "f77f2f68-1d6e-53f9-ac3a-2ac53589ecab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-y}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f77f2f68-1d6e-53f9-ac3a-2ac53589ecab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-y}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681099} :answer-field/id #uuid "02cc6a2f-430a-50fd-a77a-a216c6e046a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc89577-ab4d-579a-a446-de46b95834ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&y^2e^{-y}\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681023} {:answer/id #uuid "81752172-3bb2-528f-9484-c7959a0a2193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&e^{-y}\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681054} {:answer/id #uuid "b83fd0fd-fe17-5a09-9171-8af530b77f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&e^y\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681070} {:answer/id #uuid "d3db6582-9967-592a-adbb-0fe1ff29e47f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&1\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81752172-3bb2-528f-9484-c7959a0a2193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&e^{-y}\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681054} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ad9a32b-bc3a-52dd-964a-c0240fcb6cc5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f3a1276-a59b-5b7e-a0f0-fb6e4b6e7957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681031} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac3223b-f223-50ae-a8b1-f24ec064462e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681059} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f05709-0876-5931-9ab9-1b85151653ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681064} {:answer/id #uuid "da4a5ed7-3ff8-5af2-ba04-efc8bd553f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f05709-0876-5931-9ab9-1b85151653ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681064} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5249afd-5e29-555b-9d66-5011385caabe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec002adb-9111-59ec-9edd-86ddca0c8fc6" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor depending only on $y$ for\n\n$$\n\\left(2xy(1-y)-x^2y\\right)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2y(x+y)\n$$\n\nWork on the domain $x>0$, $y>0$.\n\nRewrite the equation as $P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0$, with $P=2y(x+y)$. Compute the ratio and simplify before choosing:\n\n$$\n\\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nUse this ratio to choose an integrating factor:\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nChoose the exact differential equation obtained after multiplying and simplifying:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging and multiplying by $\\mathrm{d}x$ gives\n\n$$\n2y(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(2xy(1-y)-x^2y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2y(x+y) \\\\ Q&=2xy(1-y)-x^2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=2x+4y \\\\ Q_x&=2y(1-y)-2xy \\\\ P_y-Q_x&=2x+2y+2y^2+2xy \\\\ &=2(x+y)(1+y) \\\\ \\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}&=\\frac{2(x+y)(1+y)}{2y(x+y)}=1+\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain makes $y$ and $x+y$ nonzero, so the cancellation is valid. The result depends only on $y$. Applying the condition on $y$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\left(1+\\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp(-y-\\ln y) \\\\ &=\\frac{e^{-y}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe choose the nonzero constant multiplier as $1$. Multiplying and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&e^{-y}\\, [\\\\ &\\quad 2(x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+x(2-2y-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo verify, let $\\widetilde P=2(x+y)e^{-y}$ and $\\widetilde Q=(2x(1-y)-x^2)e^{-y}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\widetilde P_y=2(1-x-y)e^{-y}=\\widetilde Q_x\n$$\n\nso the transformed equation is exact. No solution of the exact ODE is needed."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20afbc30-cc4d-5eca-bbbe-9a27003fdf17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 y^{3}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681262} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8ccfa8-6abb-531a-8b83-79d48335fcdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 y^{2}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681280} {:answer/id #uuid "a69b1732-4ce5-513e-8df8-bd418ea41343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 y^{2}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681322} {:answer/id #uuid "eecb15be-1af8-55b4-bbed-40c5b8b9293e"