d #edb/ref 17592186681595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2df56730-eb85-5281-bf27-f5c06a6e2c6c" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=- 4 x y + 7 x\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=4 x y - 7 x,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(4 x y - 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=4 x y - 7 x,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(4 x y - 7 x)=4 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(4 x-(0)) \\\\ &=4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (4 x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(2 x^{2}) \\\\ &=e^{2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((4 x y - 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{2 x^{2}}((4 x y - 7 x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2f8658-9f66-51e5-8de3-853f78683d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681403} {:answer/id #uuid "1c34c940-49ed-5266-9367-e8d096198319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681414} {:answer/id #uuid "3d597051-4dae-5b69-9050-725561f4361d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681433} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6dcbe9-8a64-5ca7-972a-783cd6a28d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c34c940-49ed-5266-9367-e8d096198319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681414} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cd6885-ed5f-53b3-aa4f-b4e36a2d6d96" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681447} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105c8e1f-49e7-55c4-962a-eeca040c53cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{d}x-(- 2 y - 7)\\,\\text{d}y=0" 