x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 y + 5,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(6 y + 5)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=6 y + 5,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(6 y + 5)=6 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(6-(0)) \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(6 x) \\\\ &=e^{6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((6 y + 5)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{6 x}((6 y + 5)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a485ca9-1beb-55c6-ba79-b56e18bf417b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681412} {:answer/id #uuid "29a0fa39-fbea-5ee4-af03-6c3961942857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681425} {:answer/id #uuid "59086ac6-2bc5-5396-8552-0d70b5ea2f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681454} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e3aea0-2db8-5493-bfcf-c9c1ea60c04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59086ac6-2bc5-5396-8552-0d70b5ea2f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681454} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ddab23-3229-507f-aa61-89d6f6160458" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2f0cfe-56fd-533f-adaf-6c3e31fba8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681402} {:answer/id #uuid "43d0adbb-b4de-5cd0-bccf-8c9f902ca47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681437} {:answer/id #uuid "cc