ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681675} {:answer/id #uuid "341dd57d-a023-5ea8-a479-4a2b775ea18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681713} {:answer/id #uuid "ba5b11f4-c51f-5f49-8dda-9e54d30e018c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 y^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681800} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c03d71-f742-5249-bb6c-e23c28da60c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c03d71-f742-5249-bb6c-e23c28da60c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681818} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa32167-34ad-5b7a-a8ec-f69fa6c12eae" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "390e30bc-20c1-54d5-b056-c77e888c15eb" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor to convert the following differential equation into an **exact equation**. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$$\n\\left(2 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0,\\qquad y>0\n$$\n\nFor an equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nHere $\\exp(y)$ denotes $e^y$.\n\nDenote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2 y^{2},\\qquad Q(x,y)=2 x y\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-3}}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\nFor this equation,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nThis depends on $y$ only, so\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nMultiplying gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "For an equation in differential form, the condition is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)=h(y)\n$$\n\nwith $h(y)$ independent of $x$. Then\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)\n$$\n\nSet\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=2 y^{2},\\qquad Q(x,y)=2 x y\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(2 y^{2}\\right)=4 y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x y\\right)=2 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{2 y^{2}}\\left[\\left(4 y\\right)-\\left(2 y\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe ratio depends on $y$ only. On the stated domain,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\left(\\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe choose the arbitrary nonzero constant multiplier to be $1$. Here $y>0$ permits the logarithm and exponential conversion. Multiplying the original equation by this factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105dbfc2-4120-5a01-90f7-cc33994c80cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681685} {:answer/id #uuid "667ff9c6-93d3-51dd-9ca4-7b3463adb617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681744} {:answer/id #uuid "73975ff0-d19a-5bd8-a96e-0065a2178ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681753} {:answer/id #uuid "c73d996a-f266-541d-9ed0-5702d539e5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "667ff9c6-93d3-51dd-9ca4-7b3463adb617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681744} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c528dd9-fdc4-57f7-a7ce-85afca57f267" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6945193c-0bee-558e-8d4a-b224388a51ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{\\frac{13}{3}}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(3 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681746} {:answer/id #uuid "a6181927-056b-5bff-9795-e17a0b2e111b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{\\frac{4}{3}}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(3 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\lef