 :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{\\frac{2}{y}}}{y^{3}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681799} {:answer/id #uuid "ea870d6a-7823-5903-96ad-67e85f9ad2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- \\frac{2}{y}}}{y^{4}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9530be17-4b56-59dd-9f18-001e6f0cc214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- \\frac{2}{y}}}{y^{3}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681773} :answer-field/id #uuid "db47ff68-857d-5b16-80b7-be6974c57074" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a6b10054-6534-5ef2-a5a0-f8267140dcd5" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor to convert the following differential equation into an **exact equation**. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$$\n\\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0,\\qquad y>0\n$$\n\nFor an equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nHere $\\exp(y)$ denotes $e^y$.\n\nDenote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y^{3},\\qquad Q(x,y)=2 x y\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-3}}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\nFor this equation,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nThis depends on $y$ only, so\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nMultiplying gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "For an equation in differential form, the condition is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)=h(y)\n$$\n\nwith $h(y)$ independent of $x$. Then\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)\n$$\n\nSet\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y^{3},\\qquad Q(x,y)=2 x y\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(y^{3}\\right)=3 y^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x y\\right)=2 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{y^{3}}\\left[\\left(3 y^{2}\\right)-\\left(2 y\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{3 y - 2}{y^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeparating the powers gives\n\n$$\nh(y)=\\frac{3}{y} - \\frac{2}{y^{2}}\n$$\n\nThe ratio depends on $y$ only. On the stated domain,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\left(\\frac{3}{y} - \\frac{2}{y^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\left(3 \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{2}{y}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-3\\ln y\\right)\\exp\\left(- \\frac{2}{y}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{e^{- \\frac{2}{y}}}{y^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe choose the arbitrary nonzero constant multiplier to be $1$. Here $y>0$ permits the logarithm and exponential conversion. Multiplying the original equation by this factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- \\frac{2}{y}}}{y^{3}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186681789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a5410bb-2b2a-5408-84a9-64492b7d3908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681678} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd69a43-ca37-5b91-918c-ae586ce0c2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681708} {:answer/id #uuid "941c8271-8069-515e-8c3e-bbc5147dae3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681771} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc6f41f-a6c6-5fb0-95c8-fa2c4a11fcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd69a43-ca37-5b91-918c-ae586ce0c2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681708} :answer-field/id #uuid "04b498d5-354e-5377-b28c-15c460fe1760" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e51fc0-819f-5294-a9bf-09560677d398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12 y^{2} - 1}{3 y^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186681669} {:answer/id #uuid "17eaf719-fbe2-5fe2-beea-a02cd1288104" 