d #edb/ref 17592186690089} {:answer/id #uuid "705cca86-270d-5789-9b25-9d0ef95db111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 y^{3}}{2 y^{4} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690098} {:answer/id #uuid "ed471f54-f022-59bd-852a-13190b88eeb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12 y^{3}}{3 y^{4} + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed471f54-f022-59bd-852a-13190b88eeb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12 y^{3}}{3 y^{4} + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690150} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5177e18-0776-5604-8b0d-4291b388ed5a" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ebc3da2c-e34c-5c53-a949-eb2416f27307" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor to convert the following differential equation into an **exact equation**. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$$\ny^{3}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\left(x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right)\\right),\\qquad x>0,\\ y>0\n$$\n\nFor an equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nHere $\\exp(y)$ denotes $e^y$.\n\nFirst rewrite the equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\nLet $P$ and $Q$ be the coefficients of $\\mathrm{d}x$ and $\\mathrm{d}y$ in that form.\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nFor this equation,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nThis depends on $y$ only, so\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}}\n$$\n\nMultiplying gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "For an equation in differential form, the condition is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)=h(y)\n$$\n\nwith $h(y)$ independent of $x$. Then\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)\n$$\n\nMultiplying the derivative equation by $\\mathrm{d}x$ and moving its right side to the left gives\n\n$$\n\\left(x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nSet\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right),\\qquad Q(x,y)=y^{3}\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right)\\right)=12 x y^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(y^{3}\\right)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)&=\\frac{1}{x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right)}\\left[\\left(12 x y^{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{12 y^{3}}{3 y^{4} + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe ratio depends on $y$ only. On the stated domain,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\left(\\frac{12 y^{3}}{3 y^{4} + 2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\left(\\ln{\\left(3 y^{4} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3 y^{4} + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe choose the arbitrary nonzero constant multiplier to be $1$. Here $y>0$ permits the logarithm and exponential conversion. Multiplying the original equation by this factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{1}{3 y^{4} + 2}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(x \\left(3 y^{4} + 2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186690182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d60b816-8a88-533b-a2fc-ba16ec391610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y^{2}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690179} {:answer/id #uuid "28653f64-3baa-5ef4-871b-a831314bb828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690184} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b3724f-b874-5eb9-bd35-9cc995131594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- y}}{y^{2}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690228} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8a6589-0110-5e92-bbad-b9f60e5c6269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28653f64-3baa-5ef4-871b-a831314bb828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690184} :answer-field/id #uuid "066f79f2-ef1c-5575-a596-3f03893141d8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee8992c-c3a9-52bb-88fe-ffef2f66ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{y}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690195} {:answer/id #uuid "78c60e99-a0c4-5597-86ab-b1b957c02e0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- y}}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690203} {:answer/id #uuid "91f51fc8-dc0b-556d-a5db-63d68e0a71d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{y}}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690210} {:answer/id #uuid "f663c08c-2825-54a9-8b66-5caa87352b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- y}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ee8992c-c3a9-52bb-88fe-ffef2f66ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{y}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690195} :answer-field/id #uuid "95fda519-dffb-5354-90dd-19a7367ea1f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065355b9-07e8-5c77-abc1-f111b8f508c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690171} {:answer/id #uuid "3013609b-7e82-537e-915b-cc366b6ccac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690187} {:answer/id #uuid "6c72ab27-2a24-5a4e-8507-4045e0c46ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690198} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe3676c-1800-53e4-90e0-3ed3a11c5313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbe3676c-1800-53e4-90e0-3ed3a11c5313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690224} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8168856-6f36-5b90-ad52-dc3599d589f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "239fd7c6-22d6-5df6-99c0-33bafca8f928" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor depending only on $y$ for\n\n$$\n\\left(x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 x y\\right)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nWork on the domain $x>0$, $y>0$.\n\nRewrite as $P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0$, with $P=2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)$. Compute the ratio and simplify before choosing:\n\n$$\n\\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nUse this ratio to choose an integrating factor:\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nChoose the **exact equation** obtained by multiplying the original differential equation by that factor:\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Move the right side to the left and multiply by $\\mathrm{d}x$:\n\n$$\n\\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\left(x y \\left(x + 4 y + 4\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nThe coefficients and their partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right) \\\\ Q&=x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 x y \\\\ P_y&=2 x + 8 y \\\\ Q_x&=2 x y + 4 y^{2} + 4 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtract, factor, and cancel:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y-Q_x&=- 2 x y + 2 x - 4 y^{2} + 4 y \\\\ &=- 2 \\left(x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 1\\right) \\\\ \\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}&=\\frac{- 2 \\left(x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 1\\right)}{2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)} \\\\ &=-1 + \\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe domain makes the canceled factors nonzero. This ratio depends on $y$ only. Apply the negative-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y)&=\\exp\\left(-\\int h(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\left(-1 + \\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(-\\left(- y + \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\exp\\left(y\\right)\\exp\\left(-1\\ln y\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{e^{y}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $y>0$, the logarithm conversion is valid. Choose the arbitrary nonzero multiplier as $1$. The multiplied equation, distributing $Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y$ across rows, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts cross-partials agree:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(IP)}{\\partial y}=\\frac{\\partial(IQ)}{\\partial x}=2 \\left(x + 2 y + 2\\right) e^{y}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186690201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172d2a0a-5d48-5f95-9b3e-11e90c994b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- y}}{y^{2}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690176} {:answer/id #uuid "64f7c87a-9f73-5098-8f99-f9dab6781b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690196} {:answer/id #uuid "81f454db-0f14-559f-bf7c-057ce7db15bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y^{2}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690205} {:answer/id #uuid "b6aa6464-c676-57d3-b58e-f26b8edd0c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{- y}}{y}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\left(x + 2 y\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(x^{2} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(4 x y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y]=0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81f454db-0f14-559f-bf7c-057ce7db15bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\frac{e^{y}}{y^{2}}\\right)\\, [\\\\ &\\quad \\left(2 y \\l