ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690323} {:answer/id #uuid "a9193bfb-4e3e-5d95-a04f-cc14fddd00bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690362} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ff47b4-971e-5ed2-a380-fb37ee3394b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690380} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8bca31-6e49-57a3-9b46-54735c06b1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6ff47b4-971e-5ed2-a380-fb37ee3394b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690380} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd3e9eda-257f-5ed6-a17c-03b1c81bc03a" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e459ba0-c254-5bcc-a6ff-e27e0877e5c1" :question/problem "Find an integrating factor that converts the following differential equation into an exact equation:\n\n$$\n-4xy\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$ and $Q\\ne0$, then an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nLet\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-4xy,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-3}},\\qquad\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\\right)={{field-5}}\n$$\n\ndepends only on $x$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For an integrating factor depending only on $x$, the condition is\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\frac{P_y-Q_x}{Q},\\qquad I(x)=\\exp\\left(\\int g(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right).\n$$\n\nHere\n\n$$\nP=-4xy,\\qquad Q=1,\\qquad P_y=-4x,\\qquad Q_x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\frac{-4x-0}{1}=-4x,\n$$\n\nwhich depends only on $x$. Hence, choosing the multiplicative constant to be one,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp\\left(\\int -4x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\right)\\\\&=\\exp(-2x^2)\\\\&=e^{-2x^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the differential form gives\n\n$$\ne^{-2x^2}\\left((-4xy)\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nTo check exactness, differentiate the new coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(-4xy e^{-2x^2})=-4x e^{-2x^2}=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(e^{-2x^2}).\n$$\n\nThe transformed equation is exact. The general rule uses subtraction, even though $Q_x=0$ in this particular equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186690377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "995fdf85-52a3-50ec-8b2a-89f7e343ddf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690354} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bf67e4-227c-595e-8c7a-58afe835eff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690360} {:answer/id #uuid "ca35a69d-4b3e-5b44-8dc4-c83288046d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690381} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2a7e5f-13ec-53f8-850c-b5bb85af4fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186690393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2bf67e4-2