1820} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff8b83fc-5d59-555b-bf76-4fa678f92caa" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7fbcc1dc-dd71-5f72-971f-7c5b6b7f10ec" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an **integrating factor** to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n(- 4 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Take $x$ to be real.\n\nFor a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\exp(x)$ denotes $e^x$.\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=- 4 x y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}={{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}={{field-4}}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-7}}\n$$\n\nChoose the multiplicative constant to be one." :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=- 4 x y,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(- 4 x y)=- 4 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(- 4 x-(0)) \\\\ &=- 4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (- 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(- 2 x^{2}) \\\\ &=e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((- 4 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{- 2 x^{2}}((- 4 x y)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2f6fcb-202f-56af-b7dc-d06fa5dbfb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691904} {:answer/id #uuid "93edbc52-810f-57c9-bf6e-78da77143c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691930} {:answer/id #uuid "a8510515-8a41-54a1-92b2-04071a750f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691934} {:answer/id #uuid "c6827fc3-1fe8-5098-aca2-118cd3f31d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e2f6fcb-202f-56af-b7dc-d06fa5dbfb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691904} :answer-field/id #uuid "581af229-368d-5dc7-81b1-06ad5800e3cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308af5a3-f5e6-57b7-98f8-75a69866d236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 5 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691902} {:answer/id #uuid "7dcc7d47-8225-5786-8bc0-1f6aa9823051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{10 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691924} {:answer/id #uuid "846f309d-8579-5947-8fea-ac6081480ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691925} {:answer/id #uuid "fdca3ab3-953e-5148-b411-1550271f05ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 10 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "846f309d-8579-5947-8fea-ac6081480ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691925} :answer-field/id #uuid "59f0f36b-36bc-58d7-b9a9-caae29de478c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0951a3b-9be7-51bd-b65d-4b5024a9e9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{10 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691932} {:answer/id #uuid "b44e8a49-ed00-55a5-a16a-cf838aef094d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691937} {:answer/id #uuid "d48f11ae-467e-5dc2-9c9f-1c4af59a7034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- 10 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691942} {:answer/id #uuid "e18732c1-7b2f-50e4-aba5-a8be3d31eb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e18732c1-7b2f-50e4-aba5-a8be3d31eb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691948} :answer-field/id #uuid "767af81c-9b38-50f4-b4ec-f78ad1f68768" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "551e851e-cafd-5ec7-910b-97dbe7745035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691908} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc2e17d-85e5-5f65-a456-0e4e9f8c2c88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691914} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8bf8a0-a86b-50e3-adf9-a30e8337e7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{d}x-(- 5 y)\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691928} {:answer/id #uuid "dd518b5e-5f54-5aeb-9cff-adcf4ff49fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{d}x-(- 5 y - 3)\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "551e851e-cafd-5ec7-910b-97dbe7745035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691908} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d1f776-ef6f-5925-bfdd-0c9ca7392e75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "04a68063-6cfa-551c-8e91-c4fcdeb81150" :question/problem "Find an **integrating factor** depending on $x$ alone that makes the equation exact:\n\n$$\ny'=- 5 y - 3\n$$\n\nUse the differential form obtained by moving the right-hand side to the left and multiplying by $\\text{d}x$, without dividing by the coefficient of $y'$. In this form, $P$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}x$ and $Q$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}y$. Take $x$ to be real and choose the multiplicative constant to be one.\n\nDifferential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nCompute the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=5 y + 3,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(5 y + 3)=5 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(5-(0)) \\\\ &=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (5)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(5 x) \\\\ &=e^{5 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{5 x}((5 y + 3)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{