 :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c395aab-b34c-5081-bdff-3d5685335a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691893} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc2fe17-1e59-5e44-9436-d40a541e7f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691895} {:answer/id #uuid "5d25061c-99b9-5783-b6c3-f8b4f5eb975a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691915} {:answer/id #uuid "c56e5558-79fe-5869-baa7-752bc6fa41a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d25061c-99b9-5783-b6c3-f8b4f5eb975a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691915} :answer-field/id #uuid "e241222e-ae17-51a9-a3d6-1c2301ca02a7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4373c235-4c91-5e17-8f63-a2b0dd8810b7" :question/problem "Find an **integrating factor** depending on $x$ alone that makes the equation exact:\n\n$$\ny'=- 3 y + 2\n$$\n\nUse the differential form obtained by moving the right-hand side to the left and multiplying by $\\text{d}x$, without dividing by the coefficient of $y'$. In this form, $P$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}x$ and $Q$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}y$. Take $x$ to be real and choose the multiplicative constant to be one.\n\nDifferential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nCompute the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(3 y - 2)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3 y - 2,\\qquad Q(x,y)=1\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(3 y - 2)=3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{1}(3-(0)) \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int (3)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(3 x) \\\\ &=e^{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((3 y - 2)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ e^{3 x}((3 y - 2)\\,\\text{d}x+\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65488a7e-d0fa-57e0-8d1e-db17919fe5c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{- \\frac{1}{2}}((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691918} {:answer/id #uuid "6fba6080-e79b-5ab5-8dbe-a55f72ba186c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691921} {:answer/id #uuid "