 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691906} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a928a2-8e81-5b99-9ee2-6a0536d87185" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13d31ac5-2b34-59d9-beee-6a30c6d1f7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691896} {:answer/id #uuid "3054dc27-42a8-50e1-9940-561a55724361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691901} {:answer/id #uuid "84795274-c61e-5bae-a5c3-11fc4e0dd951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691926} {:answer/id #uuid "9647e584-8c2c-573a-be74-98c340622cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{- \\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84795274-c61e-5bae-a5c3-11fc4e0dd951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691926} :answer-field/id #uuid "705e88ed-42ec-57b5-83d8-882cdce49cc0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060942ec-57b6-5c0e-86dd-ec0378bbdd60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691892} {:answer/id #uuid "0ce02798-358b-512b-a69b-bb143721aa16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691894} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1fd3b2-e28f-516c-a510-78cacd82119f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691907} {:answer/id #uuid "57c18e05-fd5b-54f6-ae85-6bb07d037ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ce02798-358b-512b-a69b-bb143721aa16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691894} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad2785a0-19f0-5669-a4ab-3300635fb709" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4a0fb07-de45-5ff4-8196-467d2b3e5c33" :question/problem "Find an **integrating factor** depending on $x$ alone that makes the equation exact:\n\n$$\n4 xy'=5 x^{2}\n$$\n\nUse the differential form obtained by moving the right-hand side to the left and multiplying by $\\text{d}x$, without dividing by the coefficient of $y'$. In this form, $P$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}x$ and $Q$ is the coefficient of $\\text{d}y$. Work on $x>0$ and choose $I(1)=1$.\n\nDifferential form:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nCompute the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nAn integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand multiplication gives the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y$, an integrating factor is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\exp(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$.\n\nHere $\\exp(x)=e^x$.\n\nFirst, rewrite our equation in differential form:\n\n$$\n(- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=- 5 x^{2},\\qquad Q(x,y)=4 x\n$$\n\nCompute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(- 5 x^{2})=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(4 x)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}-\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x})&=\\frac{1}{4 x}(0-(4)) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a function of $x$ only. Choose the multiplicative constant to be one. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)&=\\exp(\\int \\left(- \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ &=\\exp(- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn $x>0$, the power rule for logarithms gives $\\exp(k\\ln x)=x^k$.\n\nMultiply the original differential equation by this integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x)((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=I(x)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}((- 5 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+4 x\\,\\text{d}y)&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
